- **Verdict / Controlling Rule**: Schedule C (DOC-04) governs. SKU NM-LFP-1200W's cell chemistry falls under IS 16046 (Part 2): 2018 / IEC 62133-2, with BIS CRS Registration No. R-41209877. CPCB certificate EPR-KA-2025-08814 expires December 31, 2026. Air Express is banned because the pack is UN 3480 Class 9.

- **Key Clauses & Override Mechanics**: Under C.2, if renewed FY27 EPR credentials are not verified on NovaMart's portal by 18:00 IST on December 10, 2026, NovaMart may automatically delist, suppress Buy-Box visibility and inventory-freeze all Deccan battery and appliance ASINs effective December 15, 2026, without penalty or notice period. Under C.1, unapproved cell substitutions entitle NovaMart to reject entire container lots at gate. Under C.3, the 1,200 Wh pack exceeds the 100 Wh IATA PI 965 exception threshold by 12x.

- **Quantified Financial / Statutory Exposure**: Air misdeclaration triggers INR 5,00,000 per-consignment liquidated indemnity plus DGCA reporting. Recall liability is uncapped, carved out from the MSA Clause 9.1 cap. Deccan must also carry INR 25,00,00,000 per occurrence in product liability insurance. The documents cite no other statutory penalties.

- **Required Sign-Off Gate**: Before execution, require:
 - verified CPCB renewal confirmation and quarterly Form-3 credits by December 10, 2026;
 - NABL and BIS surveillance reports in the Compliance Vault at least 15 days pre-launch;
 - surface-only linehaul at SoC ≤30%, with a UN 38.3 summary attached to the e-Way Bill;
 - evidence of the INR 25 Cr insurance.
